| T4  | 2026-01-25 | Transfer      | Assets:Savings     | 500.00   |

Scenario The account list groups the real accounts and totals each group
Description Each balance is the display balance, so a card reads as what is
Description owed. A group heading carries the total of what is under it.
Description The categories are absent: Expenses:Groceries and Income:Salary
Description have postings and are not accounts to browse.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account list shown
Then account list rows are : AccountListRow
| Group       | Account          | Name     | Indent | Balance | IsHeading |
| Banking     | none             | none     | 0      | 2955.00 | true      |
| none        | Assets:Checking  | Checking | 1      | 2455.00 | false     |
| none        | Assets:Savings   | Savings  | 1      | 500.00  | false     |
| none        | Assets:Wallet    | Wallet   | 1      | 0.00    | false     |
| CreditCards | none             | none     | 0      | 89.99   | true      |
| none        | Liabilities:Visa | Visa     | 1      | 89.99   | false     |

Scenario A group with no accounts is not shown
Description There is nothing under Investments, Assets or Liabilities in this
Description book, so those headings are left out rather than shown empty.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account list shown
Then account list groups shown are : GroupShown
| Group       |
| Banking     |
| CreditCards |

Attributes GroupShown
| Attribute | Type | Default |
| Group     | Text |         |

Scenario A hidden account is left out until it is asked for
Description Hiding an account is how it is got out of the way without losing its
Description history, so the list follows that. The total of the group follows
Description the list, so hiding an account changes what the heading says.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path            | Type | Placeholder | Hidden |
| Assets:Checking | Bank | false       | false  |
| Assets:Old      | Bank | false       | true   |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee | Account         | Amount  |
| T1  | 2026-01-05 | Open  | Assets:Checking | 100.00  |
| T2  | 2026-01-06 | Open  | Assets:Old      | 25.00   |
When account list shown
Then account list rows are : AccountListRow
| Group   | Account         | Name     | Indent | Balance | IsHeading |
| Banking | none            | none     | 0      | 100.00  | true      |
| none    | Assets:Checking | Checking | 1      | 100.00  | false     |
When hidden accounts shown
Then account list rows are : AccountListRow
| Group   | Account         | Name     | Indent | Balance | IsHeading |
| Banking | none            | none     | 0      | 125.00  | true      |
| none    | Assets:Checking | Checking | 1      | 100.00  | false     |
| none    | Assets:Old      | Old      | 1      | 25.00   | false     |

Scenario A placeholder is a line in the list with its subtree beneath it
Description A placeholder takes no postings of its own, so its balance is the
Description roll-up. It is shown because it is how a deep tree is navigated.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                    | Type | Placeholder |
| Assets:Brokerage        | Investment | true  |
| Assets:Brokerage:Cash   | Investment | false |
| Assets:Brokerage:Fund   | Investment | false |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee | Account               | Amount  |
| T1  | 2026-01-05 | Open  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash | 2500.00 |
| T2  | 2026-01-06 | Open  | Assets:Brokerage:Fund | 7500.00 |
When account list shown
Then account list rows are : AccountListRow
| Group       | Account               | Name      | Indent | Balance  | IsHeading |
| Investments | none                  | none      | 0      | 10000.00 | true      |
| none        | Assets:Brokerage      | Brokerage | 1      | 10000.00 | false     |
| none        | Assets:Brokerage:Cash | Cash      | 2      | 2500.00  | false     |
| none        | Assets:Brokerage:Fund | Fund      | 2      | 7500.00  | false     |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Selecting an account
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Attributes PaneState
Description What one pane of the right-hand side is showing.
| Attribute | Type        | Default  |
| Pane      | Integer     | 1        |
| Showing   | PaneContent | Register |
| Account   | AccountPath | none     |
| Active    | Boolean     | false    |

DataType PaneContent
Description What a pane can show.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value        | Notes                                                  |
| Register     | The transactions of one account                        |
| ImportReview | An import waiting to be looked over and accepted       |
| Empty        | Nothing selected yet                                   |

Scenario Selecting an account shows its register
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
Then panes are : PaneState
| Pane | Showing  | Account         | Active |
| 1    | Register | Assets:Checking | true   |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Balance |
| T1  | 2026-01-05 | Acme Payroll  | 3000.00 |
| T2  | 2026-01-15 | Harris Teeter | 2955.00 |
| T4  | 2026-01-25 | Transfer      | 2455.00 |

Scenario Selecting a placeholder shows everything beneath it
Description A placeholder has no postings of its own, so showing an empty
Description register would be useless. It shows the subtree, which is what a
Description reader of a brokerage account wants: the cash and the holdings
Description together.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                  | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Brokerage      | Investment | true        |
| Assets:Brokerage:Cash | Investment | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage:Fund | Investment | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee | Account               | Amount  |
| T1  | 2026-01-05 | Open  | Assets:Brokerage:Cash | 2500.00 |
| T2  | 2026-01-06 | Open  | Assets:Brokerage:Fund | 7500.00 |
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path             |
| Assets:Brokerage |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Date       | Balance  |
| T1  | 2026-01-05 | 2500.00  |
| T2  | 2026-01-06 | 10000.00 |

Scenario The other side of a transfer is named in the category column
Description A transfer appears in both registers, and in each of them the
Description category column names the other account. It is one transaction seen
Description twice, not two.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Savings  |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Date       | Category        | Payment | Deposit |
| T4  | 2026-01-25 | Assets:Checking | 0.00    | 500.00  |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The split pane
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario The right-hand side is one pane until a split is asked for
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
Then split state is : SplitState Vertical
| Open       | false |
| PaneCount  | 1     |
| ActivePane | 1     |

Attributes SplitState
| Attribute  | Type    | Default |
| Open       | Boolean | false   |
| PaneCount  | Integer | 1       |
| ActivePane | Integer | 1       |

Scenario Splitting the view opens a second pane on the same account
Description The second pane starts where the first one is, so that splitting
Description shows something rather than nothing, and the new pane becomes the
Description active one for the next selection.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When view split
Then split state is : SplitState Vertical
| Open       | true |
| PaneCount  | 2    |
| ActivePane | 2    |
Then panes are : PaneState
| Pane | Showing  | Account         | Active |
| 1    | Register | Assets:Checking | false  |
| 2    | Register | Assets:Checking | true   |

Scenario Two accounts can then be read at once
Description Selecting an account changes the active pane and leaves the other
Description one alone, which is the whole point of the split.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When view split
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path             |
| Liabilities:Visa |
Then panes are : PaneState
| Pane | Showing  | Account          | Active |
| 1    | Register | Assets:Checking  | false  |
| 2    | Register | Liabilities:Visa | true   |

Scenario Making a pane active sends the next selection to it
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When view split
When pane made active : PaneSelect
| Pane |
| 1    |
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path           |
| Assets:Savings |
Then panes are : PaneState
| Pane | Showing  | Account         | Active |
| 1    | Register | Assets:Savings  | true   |
| 2    | Register | Assets:Checking | false  |

Attributes PaneSelect
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Pane      | Integer | 1       |

Scenario Closing the split leaves the active pane
Description Whichever pane was being worked in is the one that stays, because
Description that is the one being read.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When view split
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path             |
| Liabilities:Visa |
When split closed
Then split state is : SplitState Vertical
| Open       | false |
| PaneCount  | 1     |
| ActivePane | 1     |
Then panes are : PaneState
| Pane | Showing  | Account          | Active |
| 1    | Register | Liabilities:Visa | true   |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reviewing an import in the split pane
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description An import is shown in the split pane rather than in a dialog of its
Description own, so that the register it is about to change is beside it while it
Description is read. Nothing reaches the book until it is accepted.

Attributes ImportReviewRow
Description One row of an import waiting to be reviewed. Account is where the
Description money moved; Category is the other side as the import worked it out.
| Attribute   | Type              | Default   |
| Line        | Integer           | 0         |
| Date        | Date              | 2026-01-01 |
| Payee       | PayeeName         | none      |
| Account      | AccountPath      | none      |
| Category    | AccountPath       | none      |
| Amount      | Money            | 0.00      |
| Disposition | ImportDisposition | New       |
| Accepted    | Boolean           | true      |

Define AnImportOfThree
Description The import the next several scenarios all read. A scenario cannot
Description take a table from the scenario before it: every generated test stands
Description alone, so the rows are named here and asked for by name.
| Line | Date       | Payee         | Account         | Category               | Amount  | Disposition |
| 1    | 2026-02-02 | Harris Teeter | Assets:Checking | Expenses:Groceries     | -52.10  | New         |
| 2    | 2026-02-03 | Unknown Shop  | Assets:Checking | Expenses:Uncategorized | -23.75  | New         |
| 3    | 2026-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Assets:Checking | Expenses:Groceries     | -45.00  | Duplicate   |

Scenario An import opens in the split pane with every row proposed
Description Splitting happens by itself if the view was not split: the point of
Description showing an import here is to have the register beside it.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When import reviewed : ImportReviewRow
=AnImportOfThree
Then split state is : SplitState Vertical
| Open       | true |
| PaneCount  | 2    |
| ActivePane | 2    |
Then panes are : PaneState
| Pane | Showing      | Account         | Active |
| 1    | Register     | Assets:Checking | false  |
| 2    | ImportReview | Assets:Checking | true   |
Then import review summary is : ImportReviewSummary Vertical
| Rows       | 3     |
| NewRows    | 2     |
| Duplicates | 1     |
| Accepted   | 2     |
| Committed  | false |

Attributes ImportReviewSummary
| Attribute  | Type    | Default |
| Rows       | Integer | 0       |
| NewRows    | Integer | 0       |
| Duplicates | Integer | 0       |
| Accepted   | Integer | 0       |
| Committed  | Boolean | false   |

Scenario A row the import thinks is a duplicate starts unaccepted
Description The import has already decided it has seen this one. It is shown
Description rather than hidden, because the decision is worth disagreeing with,
Description and it starts unticked so that accepting everything does not bring
Description it in.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When import reviewed : ImportReviewRow
=AnImportOfThree
Then import review rows are : ImportReviewRow
| Line | Payee         | Disposition | Accepted |
| 1    | Harris Teeter | New         | true     |
| 2    | Unknown Shop  | New         | true     |
| 3    | Harris Teeter | Duplicate   | false    |

Scenario Nothing is in the book until the import is accepted
Description The register in the other pane is unchanged while the review is
Description open, which is what makes it worth having beside it.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When import reviewed : ImportReviewRow
=AnImportOfThree
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Balance |
| T1  | 2026-01-05 | Acme Payroll  | 3000.00 |
| T2  | 2026-01-15 | Harris Teeter | 2955.00 |
| T4  | 2026-01-25 | Transfer      | 2455.00 |

Scenario Accepting the import adds the ticked rows and closes the review
Description The two new rows arrive, the duplicate does not, and the pane goes
Description back to being a register of the same account so that the result can
Description be read where the import was.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When import reviewed : ImportReviewRow
=AnImportOfThree
When import accepted
Then import review summary is : ImportReviewSummary Vertical
| Rows       | 3    |
| NewRows    | 2    |
| Duplicates | 1    |
| Accepted   | 2    |
| Committed  | true |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Balance |
| T1  | 2026-01-05 | Acme Payroll  | 3000.00 |
| T2  | 2026-01-15 | Harris Teeter | 2955.00 |
| T4  | 2026-01-25 | Transfer      | 2455.00 |
| T5  | 2026-02-02 | Harris Teeter | 2402.90 |
| T6  | 2026-02-03 | Unknown Shop  | 2379.15 |
Then panes are : PaneState
| Pane | Showing  | Account         | Active |
| 1    | Register | Assets:Checking | false  |
| 2    | Register | Assets:Checking | true   |

Scenario Unticking a row leaves it out
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When import reviewed : ImportReviewRow
=AnImportOfThree
When review row unticked : ReviewRowSelect
| Line |
| 2    |
When import accepted
Then import review summary is : ImportReviewSummary Vertical
| Rows       | 3    |
| NewRows    | 2    |
| Duplicates | 1    |
| Accepted   | 1    |
| Committed  | true |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Balance |
| T1  | 2026-01-05 | Acme Payroll  | 3000.00 |
| T2  | 2026-01-15 | Harris Teeter | 2955.00 |
| T4  | 2026-01-25 | Transfer      | 2455.00 |
| T5  | 2026-02-02 | Harris Teeter | 2402.90 |

Attributes ReviewRowSelect
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Line      | Integer | 0       |

Scenario Ticking a duplicate brings it in after all
Description The import's decision is a proposal. A user who knows the bank sent
Description the same transaction twice for a real reason can say so.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When import reviewed : ImportReviewRow
=AnImportOfThree
When review row ticked : ReviewRowSelect
| Line |
| 3    |
When import accepted
Then import review summary is : ImportReviewSummary Vertical
| Rows       | 3    |
| NewRows    | 2    |
| Duplicates | 1    |
| Accepted   | 3    |
| Committed  | true |

Scenario Cancelling the import changes nothing
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
When import reviewed : ImportReviewRow
=AnImportOfThree
When import cancelled
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Date       | Payee         | Balance |
| T1  | 2026-01-05 | Acme Payroll  | 3000.00 |
| T2  | 2026-01-15 | Harris Teeter | 2955.00 |
| T4  | 2026-01-25 | Transfer      | 2455.00 |
Then panes are : PaneState
| Pane | Showing  | Account         | Active |
| 1    | Register | Assets:Checking | false  |
| 2    | Register | Assets:Checking | true   |

Scenario A review of an import into an account that is not selected names it
Description The import says which account it is for, and that is what the
Description review shows regardless of what was selected, because the import is
Description about that account and not about where the reader happened to be.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When account selected : AccountSelect
| Path           |
| Assets:Savings |
When import reviewed : ImportReviewRow
| Line | Date       | Payee  | Account          | Category          | Amount | Disposition |
| 1    | 2026-02-02 | Amazon | Liabilities:Visa | Expenses:Shopping | -31.00 | New         |
Then panes are : PaneState
| Pane | Showing      | Account          | Active |
| 1    | Register     | Assets:Savings   | false  |
| 2    | ImportReview | Liabilities:Visa | true   |
